<item><title>24/51 Kippenberger/Elm Green Playground Development - Civil Works</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This procurement plan is only for the Civil Works component of this project. The procurement of the playground equipment is covered by VP2026-109. The civil works include<br /><br />- Construction of a 1.2 m mound for access to the flying fox<br /><br />- Construction of 193 m2 of concrete footpaths<br /><br />- Construction of 6 garden beds including plantings<br /><br />- Construction of 6 tree pits including tree installation<br /><br />- Construction of 105 m of new post and cable fence including vehicle entrance<br /><br />- Construction of 74 m of Subsoil Drain<br /><br />- Construction of all soft fall areas for play equipment<br /><br />- Supply and Installation of 3 bike racks and one litter bin.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 16/Sep/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2666<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/tsi.axd?id=87d0279c59124eefb6211e0dac6a859as2666s85818252ab0f4a97ad4749bb758701e4s12</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">87d0279c59124eefb6211e0dac6a859a</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 05:20:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
</item>
<item><title>Audio Visual Technology: Supply, Delivery &amp; Support</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Services for design, supply, install, test, certify, warranty and support of Audio-Visual (AV) technology along with the necessary physical infrastructure (lecterns, sensors, microphones, document scanners, controllers and display equipment)—across Massey’s three campuses. Delivery of these services must conform to strict technical standards and documentation requirements provided by Massey. <br /><br /> <br /><br /> <br /><br />The outcome of the procurement is to identify a single national supplier who can provide the services outlined above at each of the Massey campuses – Auckland, Manawatu, and Wellington. However, Massey University reserves the right to appoint one or more suppliers, including on a campus-by-campus basis, where this represents the best overall procurement outcome.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Massey University<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 14/Sep/2026 10:00 am (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2662<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 9]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/tsi.axd?id=52a4b650482149ea800ced8fbdf59445s2662s930449e3ff934542b58ea67687191124s70</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">52a4b650482149ea800ced8fbdf59445</guid>
<pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:11:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>IT &amp; Telecomms</category>
</item>
<item><title>Student Accommodation Asset Development</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Massey University requires a supplier to develop a robust asset management plan to inform future student accommodation investment decisions across all campuses. This opportunity is open to approved suppliers on the All-of-Government (AoG) Construction Consultancy Services or the Property Consultancy Services Panels to submit proposals.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Massey University<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 11/Sep/2026 02:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2659<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Sophie Pita Email: s.pita@massey.ac.nz Tel: 0277236136<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Financial & Insurance Services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=aed6354b384f45cf903b89efa1c125e2s2659</link>
